"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[60758],{160758:e=>{e.exports='# How to convert a query to a detection rule\n\n## Tool: apiConvertLakewatchQueryToRule\n\nConverts the current query (SQL + refinements) into a detection rule with the given metadata. The rule uses the workspace default schedule and can be edited later in the detection rules page.\n\n**Parameters:** `thoughts`, `queryId`, `refinements`, `ruleName`, `category` (required); `severity`, `fidelity`, `comment` (optional). Use current page context for `queryId` and `refinements`.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements (check before calling)\n\n| Requirement                                | How to check                                                                  | How to resolve if not met                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Query has been run and has results         | Call **pageGetLakewatchQueryResult** to get status and result metadata.       | If no results or stale: ask the user to run the query, or use **pageRunLakewatchQuery** (with approval) then re-check with pageGetLakewatchQueryResult.                                                                                         |\n| Query has no errors                        | Same: pageGetLakewatchQueryResult returns error state if the last run failed. | Fix the SQL or refinements (or time range), run again, then re-check.                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| SQL warehouse is running                   | Tool will return an error if no warehouse.                                    | Tell the user to start a SQL warehouse in Lakewatch, then retry.                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| User has provided a rule name and category | From the conversation.                                                        | Ask the user for a rule name and a category (e.g. "Threat Detection", "Compliance", "Data Quality", "Access Anomaly"). Get category from workspace config if needed (apiGetLakewatchConfig → `spec.detectionRuleMetadata.detectionCategories`). |\n\nIf any requirement is not met, **do not call** apiConvertLakewatchQueryToRule. Resolve the gap first, then call.\n\n---\n\n## After the tool succeeds\n\n- The tool returns the rule ID and display name. Suggest the user open the rule with **navigateWithinLakewatch** (intent `view-rule`, resourceType `rule`, resourceId = rule ID) to adjust schedule, observables, or output.\n'}}]);
